forge.endpoints.markdownDescription:
Endpoint profiles, keyed by name. Each describes an OpenAI- or Anthropic-compatible endpoint that is not `api.anthropic.com` (a company gateway, a self-hosted vLLM or Ollama instance, an air-gapped deployment), plus everything needed to reach it: client certificates, a custom CA bundle, an authenticating proxy, a token exchange.

Select the active one with `#forge.endpointProfile#`.

**Never put a secret here.** `settings.json` syncs between machines and tends to get committed. Write `${secret:KEY}`, `${env:VAR}` or `${file:/path/to/token}` in `auth.value` instead; all three are resolved at request time.

`${secret:KEY}` reads VS Code's own secret storage - the OS keychain, per machine, never synced. **Forge: Add Endpoint Profile** takes the token and puts it there for you, which is the easiest way to get one in.

```json
"forge.endpoints": {
  "company-llama": {
    "wire": "openai",
    "baseUrl": "https://llm.internal.example/v1",
    "model": "llama-3.3-70b-instruct",
    "auth": { "kind": "bearer", "value": "${env:COMPANY_LLM_TOKEN}" },
    "capabilities": { "contextWindow": 131072, "tools": true, "effort": true }
  }
}
```
